  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): The Section 904 limitation equals US tax liability multiplied by (foreign-source taxable income / worldwide taxable income). US tax = $4,000,000 x 21% = $840,000. Limitation = $840,000 x ($1,500,000 / $4,000,000) = $315,000. Since foreign taxes paid ($300,000) are less than the $315,000 limitation, Gamma credits the full $300,000 under IRC Sec. 904(a).
Wrong (B): $315,000 is the limitation amount, not the creditable amount. The credit equals the lesser of taxes paid or the limitation.
